What Is the Advanced Therapy Chain-of-Identity Software Market?
The advanced therapy chain-of-identity software market covers digital platforms and integration services that maintain patient-linked identity records throughout the development and delivery of personalised cell and gene therapies. These systems connect patient and starting-material identifiers with manufacturing milestones, product release, transportation handoffs, and final treatment administration.

Maintaining accurate identity records is particularly important for autologous therapies, where cells collected from an individual must remain correctly associated with that patient throughout the treatment process. Software solutions support traceability, documentation, exception management, and coordination between hospitals, apheresis centres, contract manufacturers, and therapy sponsors.

Key Market Drivers
Growing Adoption of Personalised Cell and Gene Therapies
The expansion of individualised treatment pathways is increasing the need for reliable digital identity management. Each therapy journey can involve multiple organisations and operational handoffs, making accurate patient and product identification essential. This is encouraging therapy developers and treatment networks to adopt specialised orchestration platforms.

Increasing Demand for End-to-End Traceability
Maintaining consistent identifiers across collection, manufacturing, quality review, and administration is a central operational requirement. Digital systems help organisations reduce manual reconciliation, improve visibility into product status, and identify discrepancies before they affect treatment workflows.

Greater Focus on Operational Compliance and Documentation
Therapy sponsors and manufacturers require auditable records of identity checks, custody transfers, and process milestones. The growing complexity of advanced therapy manufacturing is strengthening demand for software that supports controlled workflows and reliable information exchange.

