Market Challenges
Integrating chain-of-identity platforms with existing hospital information systems, manufacturing execution systems, and enterprise software can be technically demanding. Different organisations may use incompatible data formats and operating procedures, increasing implementation time and validation requirements.

The market also faces challenges associated with data governance, access permissions, cybersecurity, and coordination across geographically distributed treatment networks. Software providers must demonstrate that their systems can support dependable information exchange without compromising sensitive patient records.

Market Restraints
Slow validation and integration with clinical and manufacturing systems remain significant restraints. Therapy developers and manufacturers may require extensive testing before approving new software for operational use, extending purchasing and deployment timelines.

Limited availability of qualified implementation personnel and restricted access to specialised facilities can further delay adoption. Smaller treatment centres and emerging therapy developers may also face budget constraints when evaluating new digital infrastructure.

